      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medina%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Long before settlers, Dakota people thrived on game, fish, berries, wild rice, and maple sugar, trading with neighboring bands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.medinamn.gov/Community/History-Vision",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1884, the Lange Hamel family donated land for a railroad depot, insisting it be named Hamel, a name that stuck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.medinamn.gov/Community/History-Vision",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Medina hosts the headquarters of Polaris, the manufacturer of Indian Motorcycles, anchoring the town’s automotive industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medina%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Medina began as a large farming community, but since the 1970s it has evolved into a suburban city with paved roads and street signs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
